2213 0 obj
<<
/E (So when the user clicks the button, it dispatches an action. This action calls the reducer function and this reducer function updates the slice.  ********This was about writing the data into the store.**********  How to read data from the store ?  Suppose I want to show the count of items in the cart on my navigation  bar.  We can read the data from the store by something known as Selectors .  When we use a selector to read the data, this phenomenon is known as  Subscribing to the store .  So we can say that the navigation bar is subscribed to our store. That  means the navigation bar will alway be in sync with the store. If the  data in the store \(cart slice in this case\) changes, then the data shown  on the navigation bar will also change. )
/K [1]
/Pg 91 0 R
/S /H1
/T (So when the user clicks the button, it dispatches an action. This action calls the reducer function and this reducer function updates the slice.  ********This was about writing the data into the store.**********  How to read data from the store ?  Suppose I want to show the count of items in the cart on my navigation  bar.  We can read the data from the store by something known as Selectors .  When we use a selector to read the data, this phenomenon is known as  Subscribing to the store .  So we can say that the navigation bar is subscribed to our store. That  means the navigation bar will alway be in sync with the store. If the  data in the store \(cart slice in this case\) changes, then the data shown  on the navigation bar will also change. )
/Type /StructElem
>>
