2309 0 obj
<<
/E (In older redux \(vanilla redux\), it was not allowed to mutate the state.  We used to create a copy of our state and then modify that. We also  had to return the new state.  This whole process is still done by Redux behind the scenes but now it  is not asking developers to do it. Redux is using the immer library to do  it.  In the new redux, we have to mutate the state. And it is not mandatory  to return the state as well. )
/K [6]
/Pg 98 0 R
/S /H1
/T (In older redux \(vanilla redux\), it was not allowed to mutate the state.  We used to create a copy of our state and then modify that. We also  had to return the new state.  This whole process is still done by Redux behind the scenes but now it  is not asking developers to do it. Redux is using the immer library to do  it.  In the new redux, we have to mutate the state. And it is not mandatory  to return the state as well. )
/Type /StructElem
>>
